I have a problem with `export` as well.
My problem is the following:

```
export class MyObject extends Object {
  subpageOf(other) {
    return false;
  }
}
```

and I get `error  Missing semicolon      semi`

if I add the semicolon, returns:

```
error  Missing semicolon      semi
error  Unnecessary semicolon  no-extra-semi
```

Do you know how fix it?
Thanks,

Working on this. It's quite the bear. In the meantime, this is my interpretation of the spec, broken down by the [productions of `ExportDeclaration`](https://people.mozilla.org/~jorendorff/es6-draft.html#sec-exports):

### export \* FromClause ;

Semicolon belongs to `ExportDeclaration`.

``` js
export * from 'foo';
```

### export ExportClause FromClause ;

Semicolon belongs to `ExportDeclaration`.

``` js
export { foo } from 'foo';
```

### export ExportClause ;

Semicolon belongs to `ExportDeclaration`.

``` js
export { foo };
```

### export VariableStatement

Semicolon belongs to `VariableStatement`.

``` js
export var foo;
```

### export Declaration

#### Declaration : HoistableDeclaration

No semicolon.

``` js
export function foo () { }
export function* foo () { }
```

#### Declaration : ClassDeclaration

No semicolon.

``` js
export class Foo () { }
```

#### Declaration : LexicalDeclaration

Semicolon belongs to LexicalDeclaration.

``` js
export let foo;
export const foo = 42;
```

### export default HoistableDeclaration

No semicolon.

``` js
export default function () { }
export default function* foo() { }
```

### export default ClassDeclaration

No semicolon.

``` js
export default class { }
```

### export default AssignmentExpression ;

Semicolon belongs to ExportDeclaration.

``` js
export default foo || bar;
export default (foo) => foo.bar();
export default foo = 42;
export default foo += 42;
```

**tl;dr:**
- `ExportAllDeclaration` may have a semicolon.
- `ExportNamedDeclaration` whose `declaration` is `null` may have a semicolon.
- `ExportNamedDeclaration` with a child `declaration` does not have a semicolon, though its child may.
- `ExportDefaultDeclaration` may have a semicolon only if its `declaration` is an expression.

_(end tl;dr)_

I find this interesting, [from ESTree](https://github.com/estree/estree/blob/master/es6.md#exportnameddeclaration):

``` js
interface ExportNamedDeclaration <: Node {
    type: "ExportNamedDeclaration";
    declaration: Declaration | null;
    specifiers: [ ExportSpecifier ];
    source: Literal | null;
}
```

> Note: Having `declaration` populated with non-empty `specifiers` or non-null `source` results in an invalid state.

If `declaration` and (`specifiers`, `source`) are mutually exclusive, why are they the same node?

_Edit: `ExportDefaultDeclaration` may have a semicolon if its child is an expression._

issue.body:
The `no-extra-semi` rule warns about the following code:

``` js
export default function() {};
```

Testcase on current master:

``` js
eslintTester.addRuleTest("lib/rules/no-extra-semi", {
    valid: [
        // ...
        {
            code: "export default function () {};",
            ecmaFeatures: { modules: true }
        }
        // ...
    ]
});
```

throws the following assertion error:

```
1) no-extra-semi export default function () {};:
     AssertionError: Should have no errors but had 1: [ { ruleId: 'no-extra-semi',
    severity: 1,
    message: 'Unnecessary semicolon.',
    line: 1,
    column: 30,
    nodeType: 'EmptyStatement',
    source: 'export default function () {};' } ]: expected 1 to equal 0
```

If I export a variable (e.g. `export default foo;`) instead of a function expression I got no error.

---

Is this a bug in the parser because the semicolon after the export statement is represented as an `EmptySatement`?

In the following code, no semicolons should be considered missing,
and all of A,B,C,D should be considered declared.

```
export function A() {}
export class B {}
export default function C() {}
export default class D {}

var x = [A, B, C, D];
```

This should fix #215.

The approach here of parsing functions and classes as statements seems to work.

See also;
- [`export` language grammar](http://www.ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-exports)
- [Discussion of semicolons over at eslint](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/2194)

