This appears to have had a regression, unless I'm doing something wrong. I'm running into the message using latest `gulp-eslint`, but am also able to reproduce it with `eslint` standalone.

```
// test.js
export default class {};

// config.json
{
    "env": {
      "es6": true
    },
    "ecmaFeatures": {
      "modules": true
    },
    "rules": {
        "no-extra-semi": 2
    }
}

$ eslint --version
v1.10.1
$ eslint --no-eslintrc --config config.json test.js
test.js
  1:24  error  Unnecessary semicolon  no-extra-semi

✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)
```
